948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}).$\n\n$14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =7\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba5df604d4ec4d57fa20c1c7f183e0d2d8c2f4f74c8e60679ef59b5fe8918388" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba5df604d4ec4d57fa20c1c7f183e0d2d8c2f4f74c8e60679ef59b5fe8918388" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f21c4e959643b74f4a8745477363225d207b247a57dafa2d96eba6b8423755" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/example-3614.json" "file_sha256" "e1ff74ba507a92af0b870e189c829c412d258fd27d779f482e4f657c64e184c7" "basis" 549 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/state.json" "file_sha256" "9b7f9219649ce8f1e238630005608d30aa9d3d81391d0b2da1b85156b0151f7a" "basis" 604 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nRewriting the given expression using the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/state.json" "file_sha256" "9b7f9219649ce8f1e238630005608d30aa9d3d81391d0b2da1b85156b0151f7a" "basis" 604 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "194faf6b71231e956ac45219686573b9a4d33f3e89fcb4add481903ef6b402ca" "basis" 604 "veri