capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96287fa82e8ee1c94c433c206151cc0784b66e30617233fb7a2b93e261a66c3"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}).$\n\n$14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =7\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96287fa82e8ee1c94c433c206151cc0784b66e30617233fb7a2b93e261a66c3"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327763" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-76643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-76643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4b