g $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-24781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96287fa82e8ee1c94c433c206151cc0784b66e30617233fb7a2b93e261a66c3"} {"question" "q-24781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-24781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-24781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-328087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-328087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-328087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96287fa82e8ee1c94c433c206151cc0784b66e30617233fb7a2b93e261a66c3"} {"question" "q-328087" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-328087" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-76660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$6\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{7})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac