 "q-327716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96287fa82e8ee1c94c433c206151cc0784b66e30617233fb7a2b93e261a66c3"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-327716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96287fa82e8ee1c94c433c206151cc0784b66e30617233fb7a2b93e261a66c3"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f7f6ff176d917a4ba88e288364baec356633e9fa45243a875ce336f40e41e06"} {"question" "e-3614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3614.json" "file_sha256" "e1ff74ba507a92af0b870e189c829c412d258fd27d779f482e4f657c64e184c7"} {"question" "e-3614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3614.json" "file_sha256" "e1ff74ba507a92af0b870e189c829c412d258fd27d779f482e4f657c64e184c7"} {"question" "e-3619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3619.json" "file_sha256" "8a7ee392e973cfbe9a6dd2b06a1994e60b3a50cb853a49686cd38380d0672f4c"} {"question" "e-3619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡{25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3619.json" "file_sha256" "8a7ee392e973cfbe9a6dd2b06a1994e60b3a50cb853a49686cd38380d0672f4c"} {"question" "e-3623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3623.json" "file_sha256" "ce7b11fea32936eaa744974a81836aea2323e57540cbb5e9e9d1851ef0d7674a"} {"question" "e-3623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by $\\dfrac 1 2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)} } = 3 \\left( \\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3623.json" "file_sha256" "ce7b11fea32936eaa744974a81836aea2323e57540cbb5e9e9d1851ef0d7674a"} {"question" "e-3618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3618.json" "file_sha256" "75f226a8344414de789f8e0b074e1466ff6e73cee66ffd84af8935bf30ed21f5"} {"question" "e-3618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/example-3618.json" "file_sha256" "75f226a8344414de789f8e0b074e1466ff6e73cee66ffd84af8935bf30ed21f5"}] "usage" {"q-7676" [] "q-327763" [] "q-7305" [] "e-3619" [] "q-24642" [] "q-120029" [] "e-3614" [] "q-120088" [] "q-120087" [] "q-119948" [] "q-24647" [] "e-3623" [] "e-3618" [] "q-76641" [] "q-327716" [] "q-24788" [] "q-120017" []} "basis" 1287 "retractions" [[17592186060162 :question/problem "What is $(\\sin (\\frac{π}{8}))/(\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}))$?"] [17592186060170 :question/problem "Find the exact value of $(\\sin (\\frac{π}{12}) - \\cos (\\frac{π}{12}))^{2}$."] [17592186257401 :question/problem "$10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘})=$"] [17592186257401 :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186257401 :question/answer-fields 17592186274364] [17592186059422 :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin 15^{∘}\\cos 15^{∘} &= \\sin (2 \\cdot 15^{∘}) = \\sin 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059424 :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}$."] [17592186059424 :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{\\sin 50^{∘}} &= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sec 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059425 :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}$."] [17592186059425 :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{8}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 2\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}} = 3 \\left(\\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n$$"] [17592186059423 :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}$."] [17592186059423 :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})]\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186057976 17592186057977 17592186057978 17592186057979 17592186057980 17592186058019 17592186058020 17592186058021 17592186058022 17592186058023 17592186256212 17592186256213 17592186256214 17592186256215 17592186256216 17592186256254 17592186256255 17592186256256 17592186256257 17592186256258 17592186256275 17592186256276 17592186256279 17592186256302 17592186256303 17592186256304 17592186256305 17592186256306 17592186256323 17592186256324 17592186256325 17592186256326 17592186256327 17592186265643 17592186265644 17592186265645 17592186265646 17592186265647 17592186270442 17592186270443 17592186270444 17592186270445 17592186270446 17592186281684 17592186281685 17592186281686 17592186281687 17592186281688 17592186281691 17592186281692 17592186281693 17592186281694 17592186281695 17592186281712 17592186281713 17592186281714 17592186281715 17592186281716] "immutable_fields" [[17592186057975 :answer-field/correct] [17592186057975 :answer-field/id] [17592186057975 :answer-field/key] [17592186057975 :answer-